{
  "id": "ability-level",
  "term": "ability level",
  "definition": "Ability level is a person’s degree of performance on the ability a test is measuring. In testing research, it is often used to divide examinees into groups, such as higher-ability groups, to compare scores or check whether items function similarly across those groups.",
